Comment:
 Pi-Desktop is an image for the Orange Pi 5B built from Ubuntu 26.04 packages with the
 Armbian build framework and Armbian's Rockchip vendor kernel. It is not affiliated with or
 endorsed by Canonical, Armbian, Rockchip, Arm, Google, Mozilla, Microsoft or Shenzhen Xunlong.
 .
 What Pi-Desktop adds to the image, and the licence of each part:
 .
  * Pi-Desktop's own programs and scripts (/usr/local/bin/pidesktop-*, /usr/local/sbin/pidesktop-*,
    the Files add-on, systemd units, configuration): GPL-3.0-or-later.
  * Pi-Desktop's artwork (the Plaid wallpaper, the penguin screensaver clip and still, the tartan
    terminal logo, the pi-desktop logo and the installer icons): CC BY-SA 4.0.
  * Kernel: Armbian's linux-rockchip branch rk-6.1-rkr7.2 at commit 44bbd021d7808cab93d1f2d64c1f092038257576
    with 11 Pi-Desktop patches (GPL-2.0). Complete source: https://github.com/defcom5-rockchip/linux-rockchip
    tag pi-desktop-4.0, and the patches in the recipe repository (userpatches/kernel/).
  * Boot loader: Armbian's build of radxa/u-boot branch next-dev-v2024.10 commit 39cd993e5d6296635438e84f4576b3a9bf76f86e,
    unmodified (GPL-2.0+), with Rockchip's binary boot blobs (rkbin, Rockchip's licence).
  * Packages Pi-Desktop rebuilt or patched (sources in the recipe repository): gnome-control-center (+pd3),
    Rhythmbox 3.5.1, PipeWire 1.6.9 / WirePlumber 0.5.17, rockchip-vaapi (https://github.com/defcom5-rockchip/rockchip-vaapi),
    librockchip-mpp (10-bit fix), the libmali-hook shim.
  * Arm Mali user-space driver (libmali): Arm's end-user licence, see /usr/share/doc/libmali-*/copyright.
  * Wireless/Bluetooth firmware: Armbian's armbian-firmware package (vendor licences).
 .
 Everything else is unmodified Ubuntu 26.04 (ports.ubuntu.com), xtradeb or Ubuntu Mozilla Team PPA
 packages; their sources are in those archives at the versions listed in the release manifest.

